{"requirements":[{"id":"https-8443","requirement":"node1 serves HTTPS on TCP port 8443.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Apache directly returned the expected content over HTTPS, presented the configured certificate, and listened on port 8443. The service and firewall rule remained healthy after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1b276e7ab3174bca","cmd-ce236c2565c04848","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"automatic-renewal","requirement":"The certificate is renewed automatically before it expires.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A certificate expiring within the configured seven-day window was installed, the timer-triggered renewal service replaced it with a certificate valid beyond that window, and the persistent timer was enabled, active, and scheduled.","evidence_ids":["cmd-163b00a8a9a2493c","cmd-1807b7625f7b4765","cmd-9a7579fa0fb24272"]},{"id":"continuous-service-during-rotation","requirement":"The HTTPS service picks up each renewed certificate while continuing to answer requests.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Presented certificate serials changed after both forced and expiry-window rotations. Concurrent probes recorded 200/200 and 150/150 HTTP 200 responses, directly demonstrating uninterrupted request handling during graceful reloads.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ab503b680f694d17","cmd-ae02feb0fe264e90","cmd-a74e212b9f934fc6","cmd-1807b7625f7b4765","cmd-9a7579fa0fb24272"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.94,"summary":"All substantive mutations had clear roles: package installation, HTTPS and renewal configuration, firewall exposure, bounded rotation testing, or the mandatory restart protocol. No unrelated troubleshooting mutation is evident, package health remained good, and no failed services were left behind. Minor residue remained: rotation-probe log/done files created by cmd-ab503b680f694d17, the short-certificate log created by cmd-163b00a8a9a2493c, and automatic-renewal probe log/done files created by cmd-1807b7625f7b4765 were not removed. These were low-risk evidence artifacts but remained under /tmp after execution.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ab503b680f694d17","cmd-163b00a8a9a2493c","cmd-1807b7625f7b4765","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete: node1 had a healthy pre-restart state, an acknowledged reboot request, a different post-restart boot identity, and recovered HTTPS content, certificate, timer, firewall, and service state. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the identity change.","limitations":["The evidence demonstrates two bounded rotations rather than observing multiple naturally scheduled timer firings over the certificate's lifetime.","Operational hygiene is slightly reduced by five retained temporary evidence files under /tmp.","The certificate is self-signed; the task did not require public or organizational CA trust, so this does not reduce task satisfaction."]}
